00:10:46,000 --> 00:11:05,000
Çenikê...
 
Chin...

127
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:08,000
Maşallah ev dorê kavnar e.
 
Mashallah, this is an old area.

128
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:09,000
Çend sal e ye emrê vê dorê?
 
How many years old is this area?

129
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:10,000
Sed e.
 
It's a hundred.

130
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,000
Sed?
 
A hundred?

131
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:11,000
Ev dor nû emrê xwe dirêj e ne na.
 
Yes.

132
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:15,000
Ev dor nû emrê xwe dirêj e ne na.
 
This area has a long life, doesn't it?

133
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:19,000
Lê murxê berf ser da diketiye eceb nûşkanî gîşkî.
 
But the snow fell on it and strangely broke it all.

134
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Dişkênî wey dişkênî wey.
 
It breaks it, it breaks it.

135
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,000
Li dikanî saq e.
 
The shop is intact.

136
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:25,000
Welle maşallah hewşên we cama we pirr in.
 
Well mashallah, your yards and your glasses are a lot.

137
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,000
Hê hê maşallah yek ê te ye ne ev?
 
He he mashallah, this one is yours, isn't it?

138
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,000
Xwedê ji te ra bihêle.
 
May God keep him for you.

139
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:34,000
Ekîd em kî bê halê me ne. Zarok e, tu tunîne, bi heriyê
dileyîzin. Haa.
 
Sure, leave us to our state. He is a child, has nothing,
playing in the mud. Yes.

140
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:38,000
Da em kê çi karî bikin, dê mezin bibin tu dê bixwaze te bi
çi be?
 
Then what job will we do, they will grow up, what will you
want to be?

141
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:40,000
Ustas bî bi muhendis bî?
 
Will you be a master, will you be an engineer?

142
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:41,000
Doxter.
 
Doctor.

143
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,000
Doxter? Maşallah!
 
Doctor? Mashallah!

144
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,000
Ê doxtirê çiyê?
 
A doctor of what?

145
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,000
Doxtirê dirana.
 
Dentist.

146
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:48,000
Doxtirê dirana. Lawikê doqiz ê te bi doxtirê dirana be.
 
Dentist. The boy of the house will be a dentist.

147
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:51,000
Ê diranê min e seg lê de diêşin. E sekne mê ra.
 
My tooth, damn it, is hurting. Wait for me.

148
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:53,000
Hîn e mezin bim.
 
I am still to grow up.

149
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:55,000
Hîn tu mezin bibî tê textor bî.
 
When you grow up you will be a doctor.

150
00:11:55,000 --> 00:12:00,000
Maşallah Xwedê te bihêle. Inşallah gula gula tu bi textor bî
û we we erim cem te.
 
Mashallah, may God keep you. Hopefully you will smoothly be
a doctor and I will come to you.

151
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:05,000
Bes we çaxê bi qonax ol bî min, te diranê min ro tekê,
diranê min dirana. Haa?
 
But then you will have a clinic for me, you will pull my
tooth, my tooth. Yes?

152
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:10,000
Ereb rabe. Te diranê min ro mire tekê, te bi pera tekî lê
belaş?
 
Get up Arabs. You will pull my tooth for me, will you pull
it for money or for free?

153
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:10,000
Belaş? Wî ez bi qurbana te bim maçekî min bide.
 
For free.

154
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:14,000
Belaş? Wî ez bi qurbana te bim maçekî min bide.
 
For free? Oh, I'll be your sacrifice, give me a kiss.

155
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:16,000
Lawik baqil e. Xwedê ji te ra bihêle.
 
The boy is smart. May God keep him for you.

156
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:19,000
Dê, lê te te mezin bî te çi bikî?
 
So, when you grow up, what will you do?

157
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,000
Toxter, na?
 
Doctor, no?

158
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:24,000
Aw î çî çike, baqil e maşallah. Dikê doxtirê dirana be.
 
Oh, whatever he does, he's smart, mashallah. He says he'll
be a dentist.

159
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
Doxtirê dirana, xaltî kê bina.
 
A dentist, auntie will be here.

160
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:32,000
Ê doxtirê dirana... doxtirê dirana bi heriyên nû dileyîzin?
 
A dentist... do dentists play with new mud?

161
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:35,000
Doxtirê dirana bi heriyê nû dileyîzin, kincê...
 
Dentists play with new mud, clothes...

162
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Kincê wî çen ne pak in.
 
His clothes are not very clean.

163
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:38,000
Na, kincê xwe kê tim pak bin.
 
No, his clothes should always be clean.

164
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:44,000
Dê xelk cipsîna çêkî, rabin bi xwe haremeka rabin. Dê,
textor tam kincê xwe tem pak bin e.
 
Well, people make gypsum, get up and have a sanctuary for
yourself. Well, a doctor's clothes must always be clean.

165
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:48,000
Maşallah, hewşên we hewşên gundîda pirr in.
 
Mashallah, your yards are a lot in the village.

166
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:51,000
Pismam, hawa me meneta vê fem nakir, tu kanî min ra xeber de
hawa?
 
Cousin, we didn't understand the meaning of this weather,
can you tell me about the weather?

167
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:56,000
Ev kave re... ev kavro nû ketiye nav zeytûnê di.
 
This lamb... this lamb just went into the olives.

168
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:59,000
Ê we, hawa wan nav zeytûna dî.
 
Yeah well, we saw them among the olives.

169
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:01,000
Ê sewa destor e.
 
It's because of permission.

170
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:05,000
Kîjan o? Yo lo! Wele kavirkiyê ewa ye.
 
Which one? Oh boy! Well, the lamb is this one.

171
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:13,000
Lo zemanê berê, lo mû gû kavirê reş, bi çi tertîbê çêkirin
hawa wekî camê yo, camê yo.
 
Oh, in the old days, oh, what a black lamb hair, with what
arrangement they made it like glass, it's glass.

172
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:18,000
A bine. Çi kavir e a bi nav zeytûna di na?
 
Come on. What a lamb is it going through the olives, isn't
it?

173
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:20,000
Ew destor jê re hol e.
 
That permission is like this for him.

174
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:26,000
E gereke hûn qîmetê zani bin, hawa çû dikaviyê û tem gihayê
berê dînin badin na?
 
You should know its value, how it goes into the sheepfold
and always puts the grass in front of them, right?

175
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

176
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:32,000
Wele pir mal e ha ev dî bimim, bes di stemal nakin, noka hil
dinin, destarno kavne.
 
Well, this is a big house, I see, but they don't use it,
they put it away now, old mills.

177
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:34,000
Gerek meriv hilde ne.
 
One should keep it.

178
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:38,000
Dê nexwe Xwedê siha hilde ne.
 
Well then, may God not take away its shadow.

179
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:44,000
Lê kî meriv nuke badê çetine. De, yek qewet gereke.
 
But who can use it now, it's difficult. Come on, one
strength is needed.

180
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:51,000
Ev hewşa mala birokiya te, rehmetiyo. Xwedê rehma xwe lê ke.
 
This is the yard of your Birokî family's house, the
deceased. May God have mercy on him.

181
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:53,000
Cihê wî cenet be. O Silêman e ne ne?
 
May his place be heaven. Oh, it's Suleiman's, isn't it?

182
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:53,000
Xwedê rehma xwe lê ke, cihê wî cenet be. Jê meşda wefat
kirî?
 
Yes.

183
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:57,000
Xwedê rehma xwe lê ke, cihê wî cenet be. Jê meşda wefat
kirî?
 
May God have mercy on him, may his place be heaven. Did he
pass away long ago?

184
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,000
Erê we xezûr dîtî ye.
 
Yes, my father-in-law saw him.

185
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:02,000
Hizûr dîtiyo? Jê mêj e? Bî sê sal in ha.
 
You saw him present? Is it a long time ago? Twenty-three
years.

186
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:04,000
De Xwedê rehma xwe lê ke, cihê wî cenet be.
 
Well, may God have mercy on him, may his place be heaven.

187
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:09,000
Lo dê riya gî giya ye, nê, kîçk xwaro birî. Em giş kê
bimirin.
 
Oh, this path is for all of us, no, whoever ate it, took it.
We will all die.

188
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:09,000
Qewxek wî nano xwar.
 
Where?

189
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:10,000
Qewxek wî nano xwar.
 
A shell of his bread was eaten.

190
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:12,000
Xwedê ji we razî be, em kê gundê gî taswîr kin.
 
May God be pleased with you, we will film the whole village.

191
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:15,000
Erê welle, jê xalûra jê sîtêza ra.
 
Yes by God, for the uncles and the aunts.

192
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:17,000
Lê...
 
But...

193
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:18,000
Ev tiyo.
 
This is it.

194
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:21,000
Tiyo pir mezin nişan da, ereban kon bar dikin ev.
 
They showed it very big, the Arabs pack up tents on this.

195
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Heva?
 
This one?

196
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Ê ne hişik in, daynî xwar. Rind e rind e. Emrê we jî kavnar
e ne.
 
Yes.

197
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:26,000
Ê ne hişik in, daynî xwar. Rind e rind e. Emrê we jî kavnar
e ne.
 
Well they aren't hard, put it down. Good, good. Your lives
are also old, aren't they?

198
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:28,000
Ne pirr kavn in.
 
Not very old.

199
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:31,000
Ew jî tirkin. Da Xwedê rehma xwe li giya kî, cî giya cenet
be.
 
Those are Turks too. May God have mercy on all of them, may
the place of all of them be heaven.

200
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:36,000
Şeref, çêcaw kî, xweşa vê gund o. Dêt paş kerî mêrekî midê.
 
Honor, how nice, the pleasantness of this village. Give me a
backrest from a man later.

201
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,000
Di derme deriyê mirî di?
 
Will you close the door?

202
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:38,000
Di derme dêrikî mirî di?
 
Yes.

203
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:40,000
Di derme dêrikî mirî di?
 
Will you close the door for me?

204
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,000
O wê derê de, we.
 
In that place, yes.

205
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:51,000
Dê...
 
Well...

206
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:53,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

207
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:56,000
Welle mera beşa nê gund teswîr kî, erind do.
 
Well, if we film this part of the village for us, it's good.

208
00:14:56,000 --> 00:15:05,000
Hê, çi barkêk derê yêwa. Em aza tenê xira di firrî dinin, o,
milletî gundî, te dîye?
 
Hey, what a load is there. We only put the free ones in
flight, oh, the village people, have you seen?

209
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:11,000
Eh. Eh. Oh cî bilbile xwu em bar mene.
 
Eh. Eh. Oh, the place of the nightingale is our load.

210
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:19,000
Çû rûniştin bin vê derê?
 
Did they go sit under there?

211
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:24,000
Maşallah jê vê gundî ra, wellahî gundekî kîbar e. Eşqil
kîbar e.
 
Mashallah to this village, by God it is a polite village. It
is beautifully polite.

212
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:29,000
Çaxê evwalatê me mecaro ne dî bî vê gundî welle.
 
When our children had never seen this village, by God.

213
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:35,000
Mişkîle ew e ku ji me pirr dûr e. Nêzîk ba, em ê tim
bihatana ba te.
 
The problem is that it is very far from us. If it were
close, we would always come to you.

214
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:40,000
Waliyê çû tarafa ne hê?
 
The valley goes that way, huh?

215
00:15:40,000 --> 00:16:00,000
Dor bere vê derê bi gundî jî pirr ne.
 
The surroundings of this place are not full with villages.

216
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:27,000
Çi ecîb o, ta dî ye?
 
How strange, have you seen?

217
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:36,000
Welle, qalind darê birjek ket na kirene dar bere froş, qene
pirr nîn.
 
By God, a thick tree branch falls and they don't sell it for
firewood, at least there aren't many.

218
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:56,000
Se kin mi te çîyo Cebel Qosyun. Ehê.
 
Look at it, it is like Mount Qasioun. Ehe.

219
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:40,000
Dextor silavê me şata rêne heta tirkiyê, heta ciyê te lê,
heta bajarê te lê.
 
Doctor, send our greetings to Turkey, to the place you are
in, to your city.

220
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:44,000
Welle hewşê xwe, hewşê roga kevnar ne.
 
By God, their yard, the yards of the old ways.

221
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:48,000
Ya nê pa hîn aw kirine. Mahfaza kirin e. Pir rokan hewşê
kevn xira dikin.
 
Yes, they haven't done that yet. They have preserved it.
Many people ruin old yards.

222
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:54,000
Û hacer çêdikin. Vê na hîn hewşê xwe kevn ne yone hîn ewa
nekirine. Xira ne kirin ne.
 
And they build with stone. These haven't made their old
yards new yet. They haven't ruined them.

223
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:57,000
Teştê kevn tê mi ji qecerin terine awe.
 
I see you bring out old things like the Qecers.

224
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:58,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

225
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

226
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:03,000
Gundekî wa, gundekî wa hey hey...
 
What a village, what a village, wow!

227
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:05,000
Ne ha..
 
No, no...

228
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:08,000
Min tiştek ferq kir ku ev gund hemû hewş e ha!
 
I noticed something, this whole village consists of
courtyards!

229
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:11,000
Na, ev kelaxê me kelaxê xirabe ye.
 
No, this old house of ours is ruined.

230
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:12,000
We kelaxê wa ne.
 
Your ruined houses.

231
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,000
Belê, xirabe ye.
 
Yes, it's ruined.

232
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,000
Bêje!
 
Say it!

233
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:15,000
Paşê.. Paşê..
 
Then... Then...

234
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:16,000
Paşê!
 
Then!

235
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:18,000
Paşê gund ha e.
 
Then here is the village.

236
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:19,000
Ewe..
 
Yeah...

237
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:20,000
Firin ha.
 
The bakery is here.

238
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:23,000
Firin da. Û ev camêe bi dubê dar ne an...
 
There is the bakery. And did those people plant trees in
twos or...

239
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:24,000
Na, her kes darê ber xwe ye.
 
No, everyone planted the tree in front of their house.

240
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,000
Her kes darê ber xwe?
 
Everyone planted the tree in front of their house?

241
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:26,000
Her kes darê ber xwe.
 
Everyone planted the tree in front of their house.

242
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:30,000
Gund niha rûyê malek darê ber.. dubê ev kes diçe...
 
The village now, in front of a house there's a tree... it
means if this person goes...

243
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:32,000
Mesela gulek yekî didin darê ber...
 
For example, they give a flower to the tree in front...

244
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:34,000
Gund niha wiha dikin ne?
 
Does the village do it like this now?

245
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:36,000
Tê bîrî min miamele wiha dikirin miamele.
 
I remember they used to trade like this, trade.

246
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,000
Her gund ha... fasîle we ye.
 
Every village here... its structure is like that.

247
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:43,000
Mesela orî dubo tê, ta naçiyê, te pere didan wî... yekî yek
bedelî te diçû... dikirin dubê.
 
For example, if someone came twice, until you went, you paid
him... someone went instead of you... they made it twice.

248
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:45,000
Wele mişkîle ye.
 
Well, it's a problem.

249
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:49,000
Tu bihare erê, rû bi rû hesab re me re ne, erê wele..
 
In the spring, yeah, we have face-to-face accounts, yeah
really...

250
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:51,000
Onû hewşe hewşe vekî barne... mezin in ne?
 
And those courtyards like that... they are big, right?

251
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Hewşê vî gundî jî ey gîhha mezin in, fere ne...
 
The courtyards of this village are all big, they are
spacious...

252
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:57,000
Na wekî gundên ha ne, ku tim ber pozê hev da digirin.
 
Not like those other villages, where they always build right
under each other's noses.

253
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:00,000
Ne, gundê me hewşê we giha fere ne.
 
No, the courtyards of our village are all spacious.

254
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:03,000
De noko piçekî wajî keriya rinde..
 
So now, a little bit more, it's good...

255
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:08,000
Maşalah. Sa peş xênî ve onû mole dar dûr ve xwiyaten.
 
Mashallah. Look behind the houses, those trees far away are
visible.

256
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:10,000
Bilind e? Xwiyê we?
 
It's tall? Is it visible?

257
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:12,000
Ka em herin çilkê latoka jor ve çêkin, were ez û tu herin.
 
Let's go up the hill and check it out, come, you and me.

258
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:16,000
Erê evol naha ev, ev jî kaniyê ye ha, ev jî kaniyê te.
 
Yeah, first now this, this is the spring too, this is your
spring.

259
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:18,000
Teba bi dînamoyê ça dikin vira ne wa xal?
 
Well, how do they do it with the dynamo here, isn't it so,
uncle?

260
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:19,000
Bê dînamo der têne.
 
It comes out without a dynamo.

261
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:23,000
Xene fî ye bidon ey medxe, yanî dînamo der tê tenê?
 
It's a tap without any pump, meaning it comes out just like
that without a dynamo?

262
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:25,000
Me dî dînamoyê dîtin ne ser...
 
We saw the dynamos on it...

263
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:27,000
Ew ro çêdike jêr...
 
That one makes it go down...

264
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:33,000
Ê we jî vê dînamoyê ye? E rind e.
 
And this one is with this dynamo? That's good.

265
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:38,000
Ox... Ew ava bîst û çar saeta ye?
 
Oh... Is this water running twenty-four hours?

266
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:40,000
Tim e... havîn û zivistan... sal heta sal e.
 
Always... summer and winter... from year to year.

267
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:42,000
Çend e? Sal heta salê.
 
How much? From year to year.

268
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:47,000
Ev av, ev nêmeta ji kaniyê tê... Ez ê naha kaniyê pêş wê
kim.
 
This water, this blessing comes from the spring... I will
show you the spring now.

269
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:51,000
Bê dînamo ye.. wa naha kî sal diwazde meh ev av ha tê ye..
 
It's without a dynamo... like right now, twelve months a
year this water flows...

270
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:54,000
Nêmet e.. paqij, zelal e.. bes e..
 
It's a blessing... it's clean, clear... that's enough...

271
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:58,000
Vî gundî jî, me go, xêr berî vî gundî pir e.. gundekî xweş
e..
 
And this village, we said, there is a lot of good in this
village... it's a nice village...

272
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:00,000
Miletî tê da jî kîbar e.
 
The people in it are kind.

273
